/tokens/build

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# deploy state -- local/secret artifacts (provisioning output, tokens, URLs)
.deploy-state.*.json

# migration scratch
.migrate-state.json

# Sentry CLI artifacts (auth token cache + bundler debug files)
.sentryclirc
.sentry-build-plugin/

# Working plan artifacts (not shipped in forks)
plans/

# session scratch (token thrift) -- usage log local-only.
.claude/usage-log.jsonl

# In-flight session state -- LOCAL ONLY (2026-07-25).
#
# These two were previously NOT gitignored, on the rule "TRACKED on working branches
# (must survive a fresh remote container), never merged to main" (ADR-019 / V2-006).
# That rule asked for a state git cannot hold: the only way to be tracked on a branch
# and absent from main is to remember to strip them at every merge. It failed three
# times -- 4b73206 "D1 recurrence", then twice more in the 2026-07-25 cleanup, where
# `git rm --cached` + `git add -A` silently re-staged them and `git commit -- <path>`
# re-added them from the working tree. Every generic tool (add -A, commit by path,
# the stop hook's untracked-file check) pushes toward the failure. A fork then
# inherited the TEMPLATE's closed-program status as its own starting point.
#
# What is given up: they no longer survive a fresh remote container mid-program.
# Mitigated -- .claude/hooks/session-start.sh regenerates a valid skeleton when either
# is absent (V2-006), and DURABLE knowledge was never supposed to live here: it belongs
# in docs/agent-memory.md, which IS tracked, DOES reach main, and forks inherit.
# If you find yourself wanting to commit these, the content belongs in agent-memory.
#
# scripts/ship.mjs keeps its `session-state` gate as the backstop for any clone that
# still has them tracked from before this change.
docs/SESSION-HANDOFF.md
docs/session-state.json

# /sync-from-template scratch: the review diff for mixed files is local-only,
# and the session-start drift-check throttle stamp is machine-local.
# The version marker (.template-sync.json) is TRACKED -- it is the fork's baseline.
.template-sync-review.diff
.claude/.template-check-stamp

# Generated SBOM (run `npm run sbom` on demand / in CI)
sbom.json

# Transient agent worktrees (parallel-session isolation; never work product)
.claude/worktrees/

# session-automation Part 3: the auto-spawn request is a per-session signal the
# SessionEnd hook writes when the guard permits scheduling a successor; the agent
# consumes it to fire create_trigger. Transient, machine-local, never work product.
.claude/state/

# Per-machine Claude Code settings (red-team R5). Third-party plugin enablement
# lives HERE, not in the committed settings.json: a marketplace entry pulls code
# from someone else's GitHub repo and runs it with the agent's full privileges,
# so each fork -- and the IT team receiving a /handoff -- should opt in
# deliberately rather than inherit it. See .claude/settings.local.json.example.
.claude/settings.local.json

# fumadocs generated collections (enable-docs-site, ADR-053)
/.source

# /fan-out wave manifest + its pre-wave baseline snapshot — per-session scratch (ADR-057), never work product
docs/blueprints/.fan-out.json
docs/blueprints/.fan-out.json.baseline

# playwright-bdd generated specs + results (ADR-058) — regenerated by `npm run bdd:gen`
/.features-gen
/bdd-results

# StrykerJS mutation-testing artifacts (V2-405) — sandbox + HTML report, regenerated per run
/.stryker-tmp
/reports/mutation

# Playwright MCP session artifacts (snapshots/logs)
.playwright-mcp/

# Visual-iteration captures (C1). The loop stays; its output no longer ships.
# 6.7 MB of PNGs were 61% of repo bytes and every fork cloned them forever.
# The notes (CRITIQUE.md / README.md) stay tracked; images regenerate via
# `npm run capture`.
#
# EXCEPTION (C1 x C4 collision, 2026-08-17): a capture set that an ARCHIVED
# FINDING cites as its evidence stays tracked. Untracking those would leave the
# findings register pointing at artifacts a fresh clone does not have -- the
# dead-evidence-pointer defect the 2026-07-24 challenge audit closed. Only
# `design-system` is currently cited AND present (`asset-tracker` is cited but
# was already removed with the demo domain). If you archive a finding that cites
# a new capture set, add a negation for it here.
docs/verification/**/*.png
docs/verification/**/*.jpg
!docs/verification/design-system/**/*.png
# PMS Phase 1 evidence: docs/verification/pms-phase1/README.md cites these four
# captures by filename (HR directory, org chart, import preview, dark mode). The
# doc is worthless without them, so they are tracked (524 KB total).
!docs/verification/pms-phase1/**/*.png
